<title>FRANCE: Saint-Gobain has small 1996 profit rise.</title>
<headline>Saint-Gobain has small 1996 profit rise.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net attributable			   4,320  vs	   4,212</p>
<p>    Net attrib before capital gains	4,180  vs	   4,023</p>
<p>    Operating				    9,400  vs	   7,783</p>
<p>    Exceptional gains			    210  vs	     169</p>
<p>    Financial charges			  1,430  vs	     593</p>
<p>    Cashflow				    10,630  vs	   9,212</p>
<p>    Industrial investments		   7,700  vs	   5,592</p>
<p>    Investments in shares		   12,200  vs	   3,909</p>
<p>    Turnover				    91,350  vs	  70,310</p>
<p>    Net debt				    15,100  vs	   3,937</p>
<p>    Taxes					  2,260  vs	   2,418</p>
<p>    Other charges				1,200  vs	     569</p>
<p>NOTE - Saint-Gobain said in a statement that sales were up by 2.1 percent in French francs and by 1.8 percent in local currencies. It added the figures included Poliet from the second half.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
